WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.450
Welcome to the show.

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:09.260
It is a new year and I want to talk just a
little bit about my plan for 2020 not specifically

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:10.310
about election coverage.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:13.880
We'll talk about that later, but, but a little
more generally about what's going on in American

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.680
political society.

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:23.829
One of the goals that I have for 2020 for
the show is to do everything I can to reverse

00:00:23.829 --> 00:00:29.980
the Hypernormalization of radical unhinged
behavior and actions.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:31.210
And it's, it's been really tough.

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:35.289
I mean we've talked about this before and
sometimes people will call in about it.

00:00:35.289 --> 00:00:42.640
We've experienced all of us a sort of desensitization
and normalization under Donald Trump where

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:48.470
every norm, countless ethics rules, the way
we talk about politics, the way we do diplomacy,

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:53.600
the way we interact with other world leaders
and countries, it's all gone out the window.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:01:00.570
And between the scandal, fatigue and being
desensitized, we all to a degree start to

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:08.460
see crazy stuff as less crazy than we would
have in years past or even six months ago.

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:13.049
So today I want to talk about just a real
issue and I want to do it carefully.

00:01:13.049 --> 00:01:19.320
And that issue is how do more people not care
that the president of the United States is

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:20.830
mentally unwell.

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:24.579
Or we can use the term mentally ill and I
want to be careful.

00:01:24.579 --> 00:01:29.630
I don't want to stigmatize mental illness
because it doesn't deserve to be stigmatized.

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:33.200
I don't want to laugh at mental illness because
it's not a laughing matter.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:37.009
Nor do I want to conflate things that shouldn't
be conflated.

00:01:37.009 --> 00:01:42.649
So for example, being ignorant about politics
and economics as our president is, is not

00:01:42.649 --> 00:01:43.649
mental illness.

00:01:43.649 --> 00:01:45.110
It's not mental instability.

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:47.110
It's two different things.

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:53.450
Being a cheater in relationships and golf
and business is not mental illness.

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:56.950
Being an immoral person is not mental illness.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:05.049
Lacking empathy is not mental illness, but
these things can be connected to mental illness.

00:02:05.049 --> 00:02:10.869
And the fact that too many people seem uninterested
in recognizing that Donald Trump is mentally

00:02:10.869 --> 00:02:15.220
unwell is a very bad sign for society.

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:21.180
There's a recent piece in salon that I encourage
you to read, uh, by Chauncey de Vega, where

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:27.630
Chauncey says, six societies normalize the
abberant and abhorrent behavior of their leaders

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:29.440
and other elites.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:37.360
That behavior in turn becomes a pathology
of sorts, which infects the general public.

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:39.440
This has infected Trumpists.

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:42.550
Many of them, not all, some of them have ulterior
motives.

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:47.550
We're hearing regularly from the mental health
community more and more about this man who

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:49.530
is in charge of the country.

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:54.270
We've heard from psychiatry professor, dr
John Gartner on the program multiple times,

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:59.720
who told us the various conditions that Donald
Trump may have.

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:00.720
These are not jokes.

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:01.960
This is not making fun.

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:03.060
This is not being hyperbolic.

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:04.879
This is a red alert.

00:03:04.879 --> 00:03:12.220
We have a mentally ill president, psychiatry
professor, dr bandy, Lee, uh, from Yale said

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:18.170
recently that Nancy Pelosi could have Donald
Trump and voluntarily evaluated because he

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:19.920
may be a threat to public safety.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:24.300
Now, whether she actually can do it or not,
and whether Trump would would submit to that,

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:25.530
it's unlikely.

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:28.800
But this is an argument that another mental
health professional is making.

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:32.360
And immediately bandy Lee was excoriated by
the Trumpist.

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:33.360
Right?

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:36.680
How dare we inquire about the mental health
of the president.

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:43.640
We then have psychiatrist, Justin Frank who
says Trump is terrified, angry, and extremely

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:44.640
dangerous.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:47.380
And that conflict quote gives him life.

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:51.010
There have been other leading mental health
professionals who have described Donald Trump

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:52.010
as psychotic.

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:53.010
Now psychotic.

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:54.320
We've got to be careful with this stuff.

00:03:54.320 --> 00:04:00.550
Psychotic is often used colloquially in society
to mean a wacky or eccentric or quirky person.

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:03.480
Mental health professionals are using the
term medically.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:10.540
Psychosis is a severe mental disorder in which
thought and emotions are so impaired.

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:14.440
That contact is lost with external reality.

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:18.100
That is in line with much of what the people
around Donald Trump had been reporting is

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:19.100
going on.

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:24.230
Chauncey de Vega goes on to write in his salon
piece that we are seeing now, something that

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:30.350
relates to what philosopher Henry [inaudible]
described as a dis imagination machine.

00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:32.330
This is a really important concept.

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:37.780
The dissemination machine is the apparatus
that includes images, institutions, discourse,

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:40.500
media, political movements, parties.

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:46.420
It prevents people from properly bearing witness
to phenomena and to remembering those phenomena

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:50.200
in a way that applies critical thinking and
a critique.

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:53.230
It prevents people from being critically informed.

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:58.840
Even the ways in which we are talking about
Donald Trump's behavior sort of is doing this.

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:00.450
I'll give you an example.

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:06.010
When we say Trump's behavior is unreal, there's
an implied meaning, which is we mean that

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:07.750
it's outrageous behavior.

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:11.170
We mean that it's unacceptable behavior that
it has to be stopped.

00:05:11.170 --> 00:05:15.040
But when we use the word unreal, it also implies
it's not real.

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:18.260
It's not really happening the way that it
appears to be.

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:19.830
And Donald Trump has pushed this.

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:25.230
Remember Donald Trump said, what you are seeing
and reading is not actually happening.

00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:26.820
It's not actually real.

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:34.000
So Chauncey de Vega's conclusion is that when
we talk about is fascism coming, is totality,

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.430
totalitarianism, whatever.

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:39.260
We won't know it because it will become the
new normal.

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:40.400
Very slowly.

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:44.400
Just like having a mentally ill president
increasingly has become the norm.

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:48.731
Many Republicans don't care because they've
got, they've got their judges in, they're

00:05:48.731 --> 00:05:53.150
getting their nominations installed, they're
getting stuff done while the focus is on Donald

00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:54.150
Trump.

00:05:54.150 --> 00:05:58.680
They just pretend that Donald Trump is okay,
but for too many people, they have actually

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:00.200
fallen into this normalization.

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:03.210
2020 is going to be a real test for the country.

00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:10.220
I'm going to avoid, uh, I'm going to try to
do my part better said to avoid the continued

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:13.480
normalization of what is mentally ill behavior.

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:18.640
Without conflating that with just an ignorant
president with an immoral president, with

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:21.070
an unethical president, these are different
issues.

00:06:21.070 --> 00:06:25.820
We are not going to stigmatize mental illness,
but at a certain point when this number of

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:30.640
mental health professionals are sounding the
alarm and half the country seems not to care

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:36.130
or simply to refuse to see reality, it is
starting to infect the country exactly the

00:06:36.130 --> 00:06:38.310
way that Chauncey de Vega writes in salon.

00:06:38.310 --> 00:06:41.980
We're going to link to that piece in the description
for the YouTube clip for this story.

00:06:41.980 --> 00:06:43.860
And I want to hear from you about this.

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:57.960
Uh, let's talk

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:25.630
a little

00:07:25.630 --> 00:08:19.910
bit now about moving on from in general, my
goal in in 2020, uh,

